{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said.</b> Because we learned that the Holy One, blessed be He, was reconciled to Israel on Yom HaKippurim and said to him 'סלחתי כדבריך,' therefore that day was established for pardon and atonement for all generations. The world asks: where do we find that the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses 'סלחתי כדבריך' in the matter of the calf? Rather, it is here, with the spies. And the answer is that this verse refers to what was said above, and this is what it says: 'כאשר נשאת לעם הזה ממצרים ועד הנה' — then He said 'סלחתי כדבריך,' and likewise 'סלח נא לעמך.' And further one may say: 'כדבריך' implies 'as you asked of Me that I forgive them now, just as I bore with them at the Exodus from Egypt in the making of the calf' — if so, He also said סלחתי there."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:28.083846836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}